{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Then you shall inquire and investigate and ask diligently.</b> From here they learned seven inquiries from the multiplicity of the verse — here there are three: inquiry, investigation, and diligently; וְשָׁאַלְתָּ is not counted among them, and from it they learned examinations (bedikot). And in another place it says (Deuteronomy 19) ״וְדָרְשׁוּ הַשּׁוֹפְטִים הֵיטֵב״, and yet in another place it says (ibid. 17) ״וְדָרַשְׁתָּ הֵיטֵב״ — they learned 'הֵיטֵב' 'הֵיטֵב' as a gezerah shavah, to apply what is said here to there (Sanhedrin 40)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:57.619232538Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}